# These packages are excluded from pnpm-workspace.yaml so they stay installable
# standalone without churning the root pnpm-lock.yaml. A standalone
# `pnpm install --ignore-workspace` therefore generates a package-local
# lockfile and dist/ -- neither of which may be committed, or the exclusion's
# whole purpose is defeated.
#
# kubernetes/.gitignore said exactly this, for one package out of eight. The
# CI lane added in BLO-34222 runs that standalone install across the whole
# tree, which turns "a contributor might leave an untracked lockfile here"
# from theoretical into routine. Covering the tree once also means a provider
# added later inherits it, rather than repeating the omission this file fixes.
node_modules/
dist/
pnpm-lock.yaml
